    "### Answer 4: Rows and Columns of the Attention Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Rows:** Each row is one token from the sentence. This token is \"looking\" at the other tokens.\n",
    "- **Columns:** Each column is one token that receives attention.\n",
    "- **Values:** The value in row *i* and column *j* shows how much token *i* pays attention to token *j*.\n",
    "- Each row adds up to 1, because softmax turns the scores into probabilities.\n",
    "- The matrix is square (number of tokens × number of tokens), and it includes the special tokens [CLS] and [SEP]."
   ]
